== Mock Examination 1 — Questions

#mcq(1, [In a monohybrid cross between a homozygous dominant and a homozygous recessive parent, the F1 generation is], [all homozygous dominant], [half dominant, half recessive], [all recessive], [all heterozygous])

#mcq(2, [In humans, the gene for the ABO blood group is on], [the X chromosome], [the Y chromosome], [an autosome], [the mitochondrial DNA])

#mcq(3, [The sickle-cell allele in a heterozygote confers resistance to], [measles], [malaria], [cholera], [tuberculosis])

#mcq(4, [The pelvic bones of whales are vestigial because they], [have lost their original function], [support the whale's weight], [help the whale swim], [are the largest bones])

#mcq(5, [The carrying capacity of a habitat is reached when], [birth rate exceeds death rate], [there are no deaths], [immigration stops], [the birth rate equals the death rate])

#mcq(6, [Predation differs from parasitism because in predation the prey is], [not harmed], [killed and eaten], [always smaller], [always a plant])

#mcq(7, [Which statement about succession is correct?], [Biomass usually decreases], [Soil depth decreases], [Biodiversity usually increases], [Species number stays the same])

#mcq(8, [Acid rain damages soil by], [leaching out minerals and releasing aluminium], [adding humus], [raising pH too far], [adding nitrate])

#mcq(9, [Which method preserves food by removing water by osmosis?], [Canning], [Freezing], [Irradiation], [Salting])

#mcq(10, [The y-axis should carry], [the variable you change], [the variable you measure], [the title], [the units only])

#mcq(11, [The cross that reveals whether an organism is homozygous or heterozygous is the], [back cross], [reciprocal cross], [test cross], [dihybrid cross])

#mcq(12, [Colour-blindness is rarer in women because], [women have two X chromosomes, so both would have to carry the allele], [the allele is on the Y chromosome], [women do not carry the allele], [the allele is dominant in men only])

#mcq(13, [The thick bark of savanna trees protects them from], [insects only], [flooding], [salt water], [fire in the dry season])

#mcq(14, [Which example shows artificial selection?], [Dog breeds produced by breeders], [Finches on the Galapagos], [Peppered moths], [Antibiotic resistance])

#mcq(15, [Percentage cover is usually estimated when the plants are], [tall trees], [too many to count individually], [very rare], [underwater])

#mcq(16, [The arrows in a food web show], [which organism is larger], [the order of discovery], [the direction of energy flow], [the amount of food eaten])

#mcq(17, [The two elements that cycle most often examined are], [calcium and iron], [carbon and nitrogen], [sodium and chlorine], [zinc and copper])

#mcq(18, [Which of these is a renewable resource?], [Fish stocks, if harvesting is controlled], [Petroleum], [Coal], [Natural gas])

#mcq(19, [The main problem with a monoculture is that], [it is difficult to sell], [it needs no fertiliser], [a single pest or disease can destroy the whole crop], [it uses too much labour])

#mcq(20, [Percentage cover is best used for], [tall trees], [fish], [birds], [grasses and mosses])

#mcq(21, [Transcription is the process by which], [mRNA is made from a DNA template], [protein is made at the ribosome], [DNA copies itself], [amino acids are joined])

#mcq(22, [In sex-linked inheritance, a male is described as hemizygous because], [he has two copies of the allele], [he has only one copy of an X-linked gene], [he has no sex chromosomes], [his alleles are identical])

#mcq(23, [The environment can affect height mainly through], [genotype], [mutation rate], [diet and health during growth], [blood group])

#mcq(24, [Evolution is often described as \"descent with modification\" because], [species never change], [only individuals change], [modification happens at birth], [species change and share ancestors])

#mcq(25, [The sigmoid curve flattens because], [births stop], [emigration stops], [resources become limiting as the population grows], [the habitat expands])

#mcq(26, [A predator–prey graph shows the predator peak], [before the prey peak], [at the same time], [not at all], [after the prey peak])

#mcq(27, [The nitrogen cycle depends on bacteria at every step except], [assimilation], [fixation], [nitrification], [denitrification])

#mcq(28, [Which of these is an effect of climate change in Nigeria?], [Cooler average temperatures], [More frequent floods and droughts], [More snowfall], [Less coastal erosion])

#mcq(29, [Which element deficiency causes purple leaves and poor root growth?], [Nitrogen], [Potassium], [Phosphorus], [Magnesium])

#mcq(30, [A table of results should put the independent variable], [in the first column], [in the last column], [in the title], [nowhere])

#mcq(31, [The part of a chromosome that carries the gene is the], [centromere], [spindle fibre], [nuclear membrane], [DNA])

#mcq(32, [A family has a colour-blind father and a carrier mother. The chance of a colour-blind daughter is], [0], [1/4], [1/2], [3/4])

#mcq(33, [Which of these human traits shows discontinuous variation?], [Ability to roll the tongue], [Skin colour], [Body mass], [Height])

#mcq(34, [Lamarck explained the long neck of the giraffe by], [natural selection], [mutation], [use and disuse plus inheritance of acquired characters], [genetic drift])

#mcq(35, [A species introduced to a new habitat with no predators often shows], [a sigmoid curve at once], [no growth], [immediate decline], [rapid exponential growth followed by a crash])

#mcq(36, [Which of these is *not* a decomposer?], [Bacterium of decay], [Maize plant], [Fungus], [Earthworm])

#mcq(37, [Which statement about the carbon cycle is correct?], [Carbon is converted to energy in respiration], [Carbon is destroyed by combustion], [Carbon is created by plants], [Carbon atoms are reused in many cycles])

#mcq(38, [Conservation and preservation differ because preservation], [allows sustainable use], [leaves the resource completely untouched], [encourages hunting], [builds parks])

#mcq(39, [Which method kills micro-organisms rather than merely stopping their growth?], [Canning with heat], [Refrigeration], [Freezing], [Drying])

#mcq(40, [Which graph is appropriate for the number of species in five different habitats?], [Line graph], [Scatter graph], [Bar chart], [Pie chart])

